From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe14 <engine@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:09:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/21] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: save reads at boot
 and loads of early saves

Two fixes found by the robot (round 51, T5):

- The game reads its save slots once at boot, before GameData is made. Laying a slot's
  run then failed its guard ("GameData is not loaded") and left a wrong notice
  ("another mod or a PLAY RANDOMIZED profile?"). Nothing is laid or put back then:
  GameData is made from the original file, and a load reads its save again.
- A save made before the Prologue starts (the slot-1 save right after the avatar) still
  has GameConfigData's +0xB at 1 when it is loaded, so the load looked like a New Game
  mode pick: Randomizer off was answered and the save's randomized tables were put back.
  A load reads its save in the very frame the mode word changes, so a change at most
  2 frames after a save slot was read is a load, not a new game.
---
